0,Kissi people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kissi_people,"The Kissi people are a West African ethnolinguistic group. [5] They are the fourth largest ethnic group in Guinea, making up 6.2% of the population. [6] Kissi people are also found in Liberia and Sierra Leone. They speak the Kissi language, which belongs to the Mel branch of the Niger-Congo language family. [7] The Kissi are well known for making baskets and weaving on vertical looms. In ...","Kissi, Northern",Niger-Congo
1,Kissi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kissi_language,"Kissi (also Kisi or Kisiei) is a Mel language of West Africa, There are two dialects, northern and southern, and both are tonal languages. The northern dialect (kisiduei) is spoken in Guinea and in Sierra Leone.","Kissi, Northern",Niger-Congo
